  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "If $cot\u2061x=-4$ for some $x,$ then find the value of $3cot\u2061(x+17\\pi )+6.$",
  "worked_solution": "The period of $y=cot\u2061x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for any integer $n,$ we have\n\n$$\ncot\u2061x=cot\u2061(x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=17$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cot\u2061x & =cot\u2061(x+17\\cdot \\pi ) \\\\  & =cot\u2061(x+17\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $cot\u2061x=-4,$ then $cot\u2061(x+17\\pi )=-4.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3cot\u2061(x+7\\pi )+6 & =3(-4)+6 \\\\  & =-12+6 \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
